# MESSAGE: no-refuted-threshold fence — the refuted 18.1 ns per-link cost
# (AF-2 audit row 1, UNSUPPORTED: number absent from its own cited receipt,
# contradicted-in-spirit by ab-12's measured curve) must never appear as a
# threshold anywhere in the union graph. G7 is structural-no-ceiling; a
# numeric ceiling must first be receipted on disk before it may be encoded.
# Lawful exception: a CscbTarget's verbatim UNSUPPORTED claim QUOTES the
# refuted number as unmeasured work — that is not a threshold and is
# exempt. Any other subject carrying "18.1" is a refusal.
# Anti-vacuity: witnesses/fail/040_no_refuted_threshold.ttl adds a gate
# whose threshold cites "18.1 ns"; >=1 row must result (shim-court flip).
PREFIX cscb: <urn:cscb:>
SELECT ?subject ?value WHERE {
  ?subject ?p ?value .
  FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?value), "18.1"))
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?subject a cscb:CscbTarget . }
}
ORDER BY ?subject ?value
